# Water with regularized (nemo) orbitals, localization scheme `new`.
#
# One of three cases -- nemo_h2o_canon / nemo_h2o_boys / nemo_h2o_new -- that run
# the same molecule through the three `localize` settings. Localization is a
# unitary rotation among occupied orbitals, so the TOTAL ENERGY MUST BE THE SAME
# in all three; that invariance is what these cases exist to protect. The orbital
# eigenvalues are not invariant (for a localized set they are diagonal Fock
# elements, not eigenvalues), so only the energy is compared across cases.
#
# Run:   ./run.sh          (or: madqc --wf=nemo nemo_h2o_new.in)

dft
    xc        hf
    k         8
    localize  new
    maxiter   10
    econv     1e-5
    dconv     1e-3
end

nemo
end

molecule
    units   atomic
    eprec   1e-6
    O   0.0             0.0             0.0
    H   0.0             1.421178283    -1.064386617
    H   0.0            -1.421178283    -1.064386617
end
